Dial forwarded ports through the current guest agent client.

A forwarded listener is opened once, with a dialer bound to the guest agent
client that first reported the port. When the guest agent reconnects, the
host agent closes that client and creates a new one, and the guest reports
the same ports again, which leaves the existing listener (and its dialer) in
place. Every later connection then failed with "the client connection is
closing" until the VM was restarted. The host agent now keeps one dialer
that looks up the current client on each dial, for TCP and UDP alike.

